member.summary:
Watch mode (the default): AutoCAD types each input with a short pause so the user can follow every command
(). Takes effect at the very next typed input, also during a running call;
remembered in settings.json.

Turns dictated text into the way a drafting prompt is typed (pure, no Windows speech types):
measures: "30 by 40 feet" -> 30' x 40', "9 inch" -> 9", "four and a half inch" -> 4 1/2", "10 feet 6 inches" -> 10'-6", "two and a half feet" -> 2'-6", "30 into 40 feet" -> 30' x 40' (Indian usage), "1200 square feet" -> 1200 sq ft; numbers may be digits or words ("thirty", "forty-five", "twelve hundred");
"G plus one" -> G+1;
common drafting words split by the recognizer: "stair case" -> staircase, "set back" -> setback, "bed room" -> bedroom, "east facing" -> east-facing, "auto cad" -> AutoCAD.
Already typed forms (30' x 40', 10'-6", 4 1/2") stay as they are, so normalizing twice changes nothing. Bare numbers ("2 bedrooms", "one toilet") are left alone.
